# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Every variable below is optional — the site
# builds and runs with none of them set. They are all provisioned in Vercel,
# so `vercel env pull` will populate a local `.env.local` for you instead.

# PostHog project key, e.g. phc_xxxxxxxx. Client-side and safe to expose.
# Analytics only initialise in production builds that carry a key
# (src/instrumentation-client.ts, src/lib/analytics.ts), so `next dev` and
# key-less preview deploys are a no-op and call sites need no guards.
# Set in Vercel for Development, Preview and Production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=

# Vercel Blob read/write token, for publishing the compiled resume PDF to Blob
# storage. Nothing in the app reads it today — the resume URL is hardcoded in
# src/config.ts — so leave it unset unless you are working on resume upload.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
